      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُسْتُفِعَ لَوْنُهُ</span></b>  <i>His colour became altered</i> by
reason of fear, or the like, (K, TA,) as, for instance, disease. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَفَعَ</span> <i>He,</i> or <i>it,
became swollen,</i> or <i>affected with a tumour;</i> for]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتِفَاعٌ</span> is like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهَبُّجٌ</span>, (K, TA,) with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span> before the
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ج</span>. (TA: [in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهَيُّج</span>.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَفَعَ</span> [from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَفْعٌ</span>] <i>He</i> (a man) <i>put on,</i> or <i>clad himself with,
his garment:</i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَفَعَتْ</span> <i>She</i> (a woman) <i>put on
her garments.</i> (TA.)

